 "said": {
  "text": "Build a plugin giving agents the ability to speak, with a full powerful per-agent configuration console and every bell and whistle a narrator should have. When a voice agent is selected a live status icon lights up on the main application and the Assistant window. A microphone in the Assistant window: when selected, a tooltip notes the selected agent's name is missing permission — unless the plugin isn't installed, then it says so with links to install, or a hook to install it with the agent. Powerful microphone configuration with integrated features and settings that never conflict with other listening (AmberX notes/dictation and voice/wake). Voices: both device + cloud, with hooks to its settings in multiple places. Profile: Refactor. Model: Opus (web console plugin + AmberX native seam).",
